{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And to your fellow's wife.</b> To exclude the female captive. Some say she was already forbidden, and those whose lust overpowered the knowledge of their hearts erred in the explanation of \"for seed.\" We know that intercourse is divided into three parts: one for procreation without lust; the second to relieve the body's fullness; and the third is lust, likened to the lust of an animal. And after Scripture says \"for seed,\" whose meaning is even for seed, behold she is forbidden by a strict prohibition, and \"and from your seed you shall not give\" that follows it is a witness. And He added to defile through her, for all who touch her shall not go unpunished, and he is defiled forever. And in this section the foreign woman is not forbidden at all, and there is no argument from the female captive, for she converts [to Judaism]."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {0 "The last word מתייהדת could be read as מתייהדת ('converts') or possibly מתיהרת; I have resolved it as the former based on context."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:10:44.880340540Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}